<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  com.aiteamforge.lcars-health.plist — TEMPLATE

  Canonical source:  scripts/templates/lcars-health-plist.template   (dev-team)
  Tap mirror:        share/templates/kanban/lcars-health-plist.template
  Rendered by:       install_lcars_health_launchagent() in
                      homebrew-tap/libexec/installers/install-kanban.sh (fresh
                      install; its sed chain resolves only USER_HOME and
                      AITEAMFORGE_DIR); _render_launchagent_template() in
                      homebrew-tap/libexec/lib/launchagents.sh (aiteamforge
                      upgrade / doctor fix; full chain); AND, separately,
                      _render_kanban_template() in
                      homebrew-tap/libexec/commands/aiteamforge-migrate.sh
                      (aiteamforge migrate — its own independent
                      implementation, opt-in: only re-renders a plist that is
                      already installed, never materializes a new one).
                      Every placeholder below is AITEAMFORGE_DIR, the one
                      token ALL THREE renderers resolve. Token names in this
                      comment appear WITHOUT doubled braces on purpose, so a
                      "no surviving placeholder" render gate cannot match the
                      comment.

  ── PROVENANCE (XACA-1233-013) ─────────────────────────────────────────
  Until XACA-1233-013 this template was TAP-NATIVE (no dev-team canonical,
  no sync-tap.sh entry). It became canonical here because its log sink and
  lcars-health-check.sh's rotation target (a canonical, tap-mirrored
  script) must change TOGETHER, through one mirror two-step. Same shape as
  host-ready-plist.template beside it; do not move it back tap-side-only.

  ── LOG SINK: why not /tmp, why not the logs subdirectory ───────────────
  The tap job used to write stdout to /tmp/lcars-health.log — the SAME file
  the dev-native com.devteam.lcars-health job writes (two jobs, one sink;
  docs/xaca-0787-plist-log-paths.md). The sink is now scoped to the install
  root, and three values are rendered from the one AITEAMFORGE_DIR token so
  they cannot drift apart:
    StandardOutPath                      the file launchd appends stdout to
    StandardErrorPath                    the SAME file (see below)
    EnvironmentVariables:LCARS_HEALTH_LOG  what lcars-health-check.sh ROTATES
  The script rotates LOG_FILE but never writes it; if the plist and the
  script disagree, one file is rotated while the real sink grows unbounded.

  The file sits BESIDE the program (install root), not in the install
  root's logs subdirectory. launchd does NOT create a missing parent
  directory for StandardOutPath — the job simply fails to spawn — and
  neither renderer creates that subdirectory for this agent; on a fresh
  install this agent is loaded BEFORE install_auto_upgrade_launchagent
  first creates it. /tmp was originally chosen precisely because it always
  exists (XACA-0651 note in install-kanban.sh). The install root keeps that
  guarantee structurally: ProgramArguments lives in the same directory, so
  if launchd can find the program it can open the sink.

  stderr joins stdout (previously /tmp/lcars-health-error.log) so that
  lcars-health-check.sh's size rotation covers every byte this job emits,
  and nothing is left behind in a world-shared /tmp that a second user on
  the same Mac could not open. Same single-file choice as the dev-native
  job and host-ready-plist.template.

  Transition safety: a box whose plist predates this template sets no
  LCARS_HEALTH_LOG, so the still-old script keeps rotating /tmp — exactly
  where that old plist still writes. That is the common, safe case, not a
  guarantee for every order: `aiteamforge upgrade` runs update_aux_scripts
  before update_launchagents, but the two are gated differently —
  update_aux_scripts only refreshes the script when the shipped copy is
  newer than the installed one ([ "$source" -nt "$target" ]), while
  update_launchagents re-renders this plist on a content diff. A single
  upgrade run can therefore advance the plist without the script. Running
  `aiteamforge doctor` with its fix flag can also render a missing plist
  from a newer Cellar template without ever touching the script, and
  `aiteamforge migrate` re-renders an
  already-installed plist (its own separate renderer, see "Rendered by"
  above) with no aux-script refresh step at all. In that split state the
  install-root sink grows unrotated (the old script only knows /tmp) until
  the script itself is later refreshed — degraded and bounded, never a
  crossed write, but not self-healing on any fixed schedule. Full reasoning
  and the transition table: docs/xaca-0787-plist-log-paths.md.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>Label</key>
    <string>com.aiteamforge.lcars-health</string>
    <key>ProgramArguments</key>
    <array>
        <string>/bin/zsh</string>
        <string>{{AITEAMFORGE_DIR}}/lcars-health-check.sh</string>
    </array>
    <key>StartInterval</key>
    <integer>300</integer>
    <key>StandardOutPath</key>
    <string>{{AITEAMFORGE_DIR}}/lcars-health.log</string>
    <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
    <string>{{AITEAMFORGE_DIR}}/lcars-health.log</string>
    <key>EnvironmentVariables</key>
    <dict>
        <key>LCARS_HEALTH_LOG</key>
        <string>{{AITEAMFORGE_DIR}}/lcars-health.log</string>
    </dict>
    <key>RunAtLoad</key>
    <true/>
    <key>KeepAlive</key>
    <false/>
    <!-- AbandonProcessGroup (XACA-0763-002): launchd SIGKILLs every process
         still in this job's process group the instant the job itself exits.
         lcars-health-check.sh spawns a long-lived server.py that must
         survive past the health-check script's own exit — without this key
         launchd was reaping it within seconds of every 300s run. -->
    <key>AbandonProcessGroup</key>
    <true/>
</dict>
</plist>
